WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:02.340
You know your product.

2
00:00:02.510 --> 00:00:05.500
But what happens when someone sees it for
the first time?

3
00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:06.860
Meet Gnomi.

4
00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:09.260
Social simulation for product teams.

5
00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:11.660
Perspective before you ship.

6
00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:14.580
You define audience segments and their
shares.

7
00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:19.430
Gnomi samples traits such as language,
device, and patience using a saved

8
00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:20.740
random seed.

9
00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:24.700
A language model proposes fictional
profiles from those traits.

10
00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:28.140
Gnomi selects one candidate and expands
its biography.

11
00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:31.020
You review and edit the personas before a
run.

12
00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:33.900
They represent your assumptions about an
audience.

13
00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:38.100
Share your idea, staging app, or your
Figma design.

14
00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:40.140
Set a goal and a budget.

15
00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:43.380
Each persona explores from a different
perspective.

16
00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:44.540
They click.

17
00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:45.780
They pause.

18
00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:47.620
They encounter friction.

19
00:00:47.990 --> 00:00:52.150
Follow their actions, generated comments,
and screenshots to inspect what

20
00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:53.900
happened in the simulation.

21
00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:56.100
Then the conversation starts.

22
00:00:56.230 --> 00:00:59.380
Personas post, reply, and react.

23
00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:03.070
Watch how a complaint travels through this
simulated community, and whose

24
00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:05.300
generated opinion changes.

25
00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:10.590
Gnomi brings it together in a report:
ranked friction hypotheses, affected

26
00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:14.740
simulated segments, screenshots, and
generated quotes.

27
00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:17.180
These records show what the agents did.

28
00:01:17.270 --> 00:01:22.060
They do not establish what real users need
or how often a problem occurs.

29
00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:26.180
Projects run on your machine, with your
own model keys.

30
00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:29.260
Model inputs go to the provider you
configure.

31
00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:33.940
Simulated findings are hypotheses, not
evidence about real users.

32
00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:37.790
Choose what to investigate, then test it
with real people before drawing

33
00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:39.100
conclusions.

34
00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:40.700
Find the friction.

35
00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:42.460
Follow the conversation.

36
00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:44.420
Know what to test next.

37
00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:45.390
Gnomi.
